[187.908102, "o", "14:Each game consists of 2 turns."]
[187.908505, "o", "\r\n"]
[187.908813, "o", "15:o For each turn, roll one six-sided die 6 times, making a note of each number in the order it"]
[187.908948, "o", "\r\n"]
[187.909026, "o", "17:o Once you have your list of six numbers, determine the possible scores for the turn"]
[187.909086, "o", "\r\n"]
[187.909148, "o", "20:turns, noting that no category may be used more than once (i.e. you may not score the two hands"]
[187.909209, "o", "\r\n"]
[187.909285, "o", "24:analyze the resulting scores. Questions 20 to 26 require only the ‘turn’ results. Questions 27 to 29"]
[187.909351, "o", "\r\n"]
[187.909423, "o", "26:The workbook provided contains dice rolls from 6,000 simulated turns (3,000 games). Use the rules"]
[187.909505, "o", "\r\n"]
[187.909573, "o", "27:below to first determine the possible scores for the turns, and then to find the highest possible score for"]
[187.909639, "o", "\r\n"]
[187.909707, "o", "29:SCORING TURNS"]
[187.909785, "o", "\r\n"]
[187.909876, "o", "36:Any turn"]
[187.909941, "o", "\r\n"]
[187.910003, "o", "38:The highest number rolled in the turn"]
